 # Create a verification skill
 
-Every serious project needs a scripted way to drive the real app and prove behavior: launch it, exercise a feature the way a user would, and capture evidence. This skill generates that as a project-local `verify-<app>` skill tailored to the repo. Use the consuming project's own skill source for the generated skill, not the shared PSTACK bundle. Follow the project's skill-authoring guidance; for Skillbox, load `skillbox skills get skillbox-author`. You write the generator's output for the next agent, not for a human: it will be read cold, mid-task, by an agent that has never seen the app.
+Every serious project needs a scripted way to drive the real app and prove behavior: launch it, exercise a feature the way a user would, and capture evidence. This skill generates that as a project-local `verify-<app>` skill tailored to the repo. Write it in the consuming project's owned skill source. Load `skillbox skills get skillbox-author` for source layout and installation. Never edit a generated installation. You write the generator's output for the next agent, not for a human: it will be read cold, mid-task, by an agent that has never seen the app.
 
